{"html":"<h1>Troubleshooting</h1>\n<p>This page helps diagnose common <code>vix.app</code> issues. Most problems come from one of a few places: Vix is not using the manifest you think it is using, a source file is missing from <code>sources</code>, an include root is too deep or too shallow, a runtime file was not copied through <code>resources</code>, a linked target is missing, or an app module declaration does not match the module structure.</p>\n<p>Start with the normal workflow.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>For module-based backends, run the module check before building.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> check</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>The goal is to fix the manifest, not the generated files. When a project uses <code>vix.app</code>, the root manifest is the source of truth.</p>\n<h2>Vix is not using <code>vix.app</code></h2>\n<p>If the project root still contains <code>CMakeLists.txt</code>, Vix will use that file first. <code>vix.app</code> is used only when no root <code>CMakeLists.txt</code> is present.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>1. CMakeLists.txt\n2. vix.app</code></pre><p>This is intentional. It protects existing projects from changing behavior just because a <code>vix.app</code> file was added during migration.</p>\n<p>Check the project root.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">ls</span></span></code></pre><p>If both files exist, the existing project input is active.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>project/\n  CMakeLists.txt\n  vix.app\n  src/</code></pre><p>To make <code>vix.app</code> active, remove or rename the root <code>CMakeLists.txt</code> when the migration is ready.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>project/\n  vix.app\n  src/</code></pre><p>Then build again.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><h2>Missing or invalid <code>name</code></h2>\n<p>A <code>vix.app</code> file must define a target name.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">name</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"api\"</span></span></code></pre><p>If the name is empty or missing, Vix cannot generate a usable application target.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\"># Wrong.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"executable\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Fix it by adding a stable name near the top of the manifest.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">name</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"api\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"executable\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Keep this name stable. It may be used by generated wiring, tasks, service configuration, and module target names.</p>\n<h2>Unsupported target type</h2>\n<p>The <code>type</code> field must describe a supported target shape.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"executable\"</span></span></code></pre><p>Supported values include:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>executable\nstatic-library\nshared-library</code></pre><p>Shorter aliases such as <code>static</code>, <code>shared</code>, and <code>library</code> are accepted, but the full names are clearer in documentation and project manifests.</p>\n<p>If the project should run with <code>vix run</code>, use:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"executable\"</span></span></code></pre><p>Use a library type only when the project produces reusable code instead of a runnable program.</p>\n<h2>Source file not found</h2>\n<p>If the build fails because a source file cannot be found, check the <code>sources</code> list first.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/api/app/AppBootstrap.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Every path is relative to the project root, not the generated build directory.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>api/\n  vix.app\n  src/\n    main.cpp\n    api/\n      app/\n        AppBootstrap.cpp</code></pre><p>A common mistake is writing a path from the wrong directory.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\"># Wrong when vix.app is already at the project root.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"api/src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>The correct path should start from the directory that contains <code>vix.app</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>After fixing the path, build again.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><h2>New <code>.cpp</code> file is not compiled</h2>\n<p>If you added a new implementation file and the linker reports missing symbols, the file may not be listed in <code>sources</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>src/\n  main.cpp\n  api/\n    support/\n      HttpResponses.cpp</code></pre><p>Add the new file explicitly.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/api/support/HttpResponses.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Headers do not usually belong in <code>sources</code>, but <code>.cpp</code> files that contain implementation code must be listed.</p>\n<h2>Header cannot be found</h2>\n<p>If the compiler cannot find a header, check <code>include_dirs</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">include_dirs</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"include\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>If the header is here:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>include/api/app/AppBootstrap.hpp</code></pre><p>the source should include it like this:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> &#x3C;api/app/AppBootstrap.hpp></span></span></code></pre><p>and the include directory should be:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">include_dirs</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"include\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Do not point the include directory too deep into the tree.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\"># Avoid this.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">include_dirs</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"include/api/app\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>A deep include root makes the include style unstable and harder to understand.</p>\n<h2>Do not fix includes with resources</h2>\n<p><code>resources</code> does not help the compiler find headers. Resources are copied beside the built target for runtime use.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\"># Wrong.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">resources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"include=include\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Fix include problems with <code>include_dirs</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">include_dirs</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"include\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Use <code>resources</code> only for files the program needs when it runs.</p>\n<h2>Linked target is missing</h2>\n<p>If the build fails because a target or library is missing, check <code>packages</code> and <code>links</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">links</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>The package makes something available. The link entry connects the application target to a specific target.</p>\n<p>If the code uses ORM, the manifest should link ORM.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">links</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::orm\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>If the project uses the game runtime, link the game targets instead.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">links</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::game\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::io\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Do not link every module by default. Link the targets the application actually uses.</p>\n<h2>Registry dependency does not resolve</h2>\n<p>Registry dependencies belong in <code>deps</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">deps</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"adastra/logger@1.0.0\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Accepted forms are:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>namespace/name\nnamespace/name@version\n@namespace/name\n@namespace/name@version</code></pre><p>After changing registry dependencies, resolve them and build.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> install</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>A dependency entry does not replace <code>links</code>. If the package exports a target that the application uses, the target should still be listed in <code>links</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">deps</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"adastra/logger@1.0.0\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">links</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"adastra::logger\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>The exact exported target name comes from the dependency itself.</p>\n<h2>Runtime file is missing</h2>\n<p>If the application builds but cannot find <code>.env</code>, <code>public</code>, <code>views</code>, <code>storage</code>, assets, or package metadata at runtime, check <code>resources</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">resources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \".env=.env\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"public=public\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"views=views\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"storage=storage\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Resources are copied beside the built target, usually under the configured <code>output_dir</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">output_dir</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"bin\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">resources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \".env=.env\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"public=public\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>A backend runtime layout should look like this:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>bin/\n  api\n  .env\n  public/</code></pre><p>If the source path is wrong, Vix cannot copy the file. Remember that resource source paths are relative to the project root.</p>\n<h2>Resource copied to the wrong place</h2>\n<p>Use <code>source=destination</code> when the runtime path should differ from the source path.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">resources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"config/dev.env=.env\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"frontend/dist=public\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>The left side is the project file or directory. The right side is where it should appear beside the built target.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>bin/\n  app\n  .env\n  public/</code></pre><p>Keep destination paths simple. A runtime layout that is easy to inspect is easier to debug.</p>\n<h2><code>vix run</code> does not work for a library</h2>\n<p><code>vix run</code> is for executable targets. If the manifest describes a library, build it instead.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">name</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"mathkit\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"static-library\"</span></span></code></pre><p>Use:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>If the project should run as a program, change the target type.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"executable\"</span></span></code></pre><p>A project with <code>main()</code> normally should be an executable target.</p>\n<h2>Module does not appear in the list</h2>\n<p>If <code>vix modules list</code> does not show a module, check that the module section is declared in <code>vix.app</code>.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">[module.auth]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">enabled</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = true</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">path</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"modules/auth\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">kind</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"backend\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">depends</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = []</span></span></code></pre><p>Then run:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> list</span></span></code></pre><p>If the module was created manually, make sure the section name is correct and the file is saved at the project root.</p>\n<h2>Module path is wrong</h2>\n<p>The <code>path</code> field is relative to the project root.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">[module.auth]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">path</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"modules/auth\"</span></span></code></pre><p>The matching folder should exist.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>modules/\n  auth/\n    include/\n    src/</code></pre><p>If the module folder is missing, create it through the CLI.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> add</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> auth</span></span></code></pre><p>Then check the project.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> check</span></span></code></pre><h2>Module dependency is missing</h2>\n<p>If one module uses another module, declare the dependency.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">[module.projects]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">enabled</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = true</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">path</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"modules/projects\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">kind</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"backend\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">depends</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"auth\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>This tells Vix that <code>projects</code> is allowed to use the public API of <code>auth</code>.</p>\n<p>The source should include the public header.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> &#x3C;auth/api.hpp></span></span></code></pre><p>Avoid private cross-module includes.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\">// Avoid this.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> \"../auth/src/AuthService.hpp\"</span></span></code></pre><p>Cross-module usage should go through public headers and explicit dependencies.</p>\n<h2>Enabled module depends on disabled module</h2>\n<p>If an enabled module depends on another module, the dependency should also be enabled.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">[module.auth]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">enabled</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = false</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">path</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"modules/auth\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">kind</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"backend\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">depends</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = []</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">[module.projects]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">enabled</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = true</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">path</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"modules/projects\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">kind</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"backend\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">depends</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"auth\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>This is not a healthy active configuration because <code>projects</code> depends on a module that is not active.</p>\n<p>Fix it by enabling the dependency:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> enable</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> auth</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> check</span></span></code></pre><p>or by removing the dependency from the module that no longer uses it.</p>\n<h2>Generated files were edited manually</h2>\n<p>When Vix uses <code>vix.app</code>, generated build files are written under:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>.vix/generated/app/</code></pre><p>Do not edit these files to change the application. They are generated output.</p>\n<p>Edit <code>vix.app</code> instead, then run:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>If the generated files look stale after a manifest change, run a clean build workflow or remove the generated directory and build again.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">rm</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\"> -rf</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> .vix/generated/app</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><h2><code>vix.app</code> changed but dev output did not change</h2>\n<p>When <code>vix.app</code> changes, the project configuration has changed. Rebuild the project so Vix can refresh the generated app project and module wiring.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>For module-based backends, check modules first.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> check</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span></code></pre><p>Normal source changes can use the fast rebuild path, but manifest changes should be treated as configuration changes.</p>\n<h2>Compile option breaks one compiler</h2>\n<p>Raw compiler options can be platform-specific. Use conditional entries when an option should only apply to a compiler family.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">compile_options</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"$&#x3C;$&#x3C;CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>:/W4>\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"$&#x3C;$&#x3C;NOT:$&#x3C;CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>>:-Wall>\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>Avoid unconditional flags that only work on one compiler.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\"># Avoid this in portable manifests.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">compile_options</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"-Wall\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><p>For sanitizer builds, keep compile and link flags together.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">compile_options</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"$&#x3C;$&#x3C;NOT:$&#x3C;CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>>:-fsanitize=address,undefined>\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">link_options</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"$&#x3C;$&#x3C;NOT:$&#x3C;CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>>:-fsanitize=address,undefined>\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><h2>Output directory is confusing</h2>\n<p>For applications, use a simple output directory.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">output_dir</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"bin\"</span></span></code></pre><p>This keeps the executable and runtime resources close together.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code docs-code--plain\"><code>bin/\n  api\n  .env\n  public/</code></pre><p>Avoid deeply nested output paths unless the project has a clear reason.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6A737D\"># Avoid unless necessary.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">output_dir</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"runtime/linux/debug/bin\"</span></span></code></pre><p>The output directory should make the runtime easier to find, not harder.</p>\n<h2>Full backend check</h2>\n<p>For a backend with modules, use this sequence when the error is unclear.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> list</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> modules</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> check</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> tests</span></span></code></pre><p>This checks the module declarations, module structure, build manifest, and test suite in a predictable order.</p>\n<p>For a stronger single workflow:</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> check</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\"> --tests</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\"> --run</span></span></code></pre><p>Use the longer sequence when you need to see where the failure starts.</p>\n<h2>Quick diagnosis table</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Symptom</th>\n<th>Check first</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>vix.app</code> seems ignored</td>\n<td>Root <code>CMakeLists.txt</code> still exists</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Source file missing</td>\n<td><code>sources</code> path relative to project root</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Header not found</td>\n<td><code>include_dirs</code> root and include style</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Link target missing</td>\n<td><code>packages</code>, <code>deps</code>, and <code>links</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Runtime file missing</td>\n<td><code>resources</code> and <code>output_dir</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Module not listed</td>\n<td><code>[module.&lt;name&gt;]</code> section in <code>vix.app</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Module boundary error</td>\n<td><code>depends</code> and public include layout</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Library cannot run</td>\n<td><code>type</code> is not <code>executable</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generated file changes disappear</td>\n<td>Edit <code>vix.app</code>, not <code>.vix/generated/app/</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>A known-good minimal app</h2>\n<p>When the project is difficult to diagnose, reduce it to a minimal known-good shape.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">name</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"hello\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">type</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"executable\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">standard</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"c++20\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">output_dir</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = </span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"bin\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">sources</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src/main.cpp\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">include_dirs</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"src\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">packages</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">links</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\"> = [</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">  \"vix::vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">]</span></span></code></pre><pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">#include</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> &#x3C;vix/print.hpp></span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">int</span><span style=\"color:#B392F0\"> main</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">  vix</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">::</span><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">print</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\">\"Hello from Vix\"</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#F97583\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#79B8FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span></code></pre><p>Then build and run.</p>\n<pre class=\"docs-code shiki github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#24292e;color:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> build</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#B392F0\">vix</span><span style=\"color:#9ECBFF\"> run</span></span></code></pre><p>Once this works, add the real source files, include directories, links, resources, and modules back in small steps.</p>\n<h2>Next step</h2>\n<p>Continue with best practices to keep <code>vix.app</code> readable and predictable as the project grows.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/docs/guides/vix-app/best-practices\">Best Practices</a></p>\n"}
